# ============================================================================
# backup_database.rman
#
# Purpose:
#   Template for a full database backup plus archived logs. This is the
#   backup half of a recovery strategy: a usable full backup, the
#   archived logs that follow it, and nothing deleted until the backup
#   is verified.
#
# Usage:
#   rman TARGET / @backup_database.rman
#
#   Before running it, replace <BACKUP_LOCATION> with the backup
#   destination and confirm the backup policy in
#   docs/backup-strategy.md (retention, window, and whether the fast
#   recovery area is in use). If the fast recovery area is configured
#   as the backup destination, drop the FORMAT clause and let RMAN
#   place the pieces there.
#
# What it does NOT do:
#   It does not delete archived logs. BACKUP ... PLUS ARCHIVELOG with
#   DELETE INPUT is common, but deleting logs is a separate, deliberate
#   step that belongs after the backup is verified, not inside the job
#   that creates it. See docs/restore-validation-workflow.md.
#
# Notes:
#   This file writes backup pieces. It changes state on the backup
#   destination, not on the database data. Review it, test it against
#   a non-production database first, and keep controlfile autobackup
#   on (CONFIGURE CONTROLFILE AUTOBACKUP ON) so a restore never has
#   to hunt for a control file.
#   Reviewed; not executed against a live Oracle instance.
# ============================================================================

RUN {
  ALLOCATE CHANNEL c1 DEVICE TYPE DISK FORMAT '<BACKUP_LOCATION>/%U';

  BACKUP AS COMPRESSED BACKUPSET DATABASE PLUS ARCHIVELOG;

  RELEASE CHANNEL c1;
}

# After this job completes, confirm it before trusting it:
#   LIST BACKUP SUMMARY;
# and run the validation in rman/validate_restore.rman.
# The readiness check in sql/recovery_readiness.sql reports the new
# backup on its next run.
